ical grep found **zero** rejection paths: no `return` (both fns are `void`), no asserts, no null checks, no range checks, no error enums, no pointer params. Table documents the empty error surface, then enumerates 8 generic-boundary classes (E1–E8) that are tested instead.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 18 rows. No runtime options/flags/state exist in the C at all; the axes are IEEE-754 value class × per-byte value × call multiplicity, plus the single (and lowest-level) entry point.\n\n**Phases B/C** — `tests/differential.rs`, 27 tests, all passing. Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and only ever called through the exported `driver` symbol. ~350k randomized inputs (splitmix64, fixed seed) across normals, subnormals, signed zeros, ±inf, quiet/signalling NaNs with random payloads, IEEE boundary constants, every byte value 0x00–0xff in all 4 positions, and 300k unconstrained `u32`→`f32` bit patterns.\n\nTwo harness details worth noting:\n- Output goes to C `stdout`, so capture forks a child with a private fd 1 — the first `dup2`-based version was silently capturing libtest's own concurrent `test X ... ok` lines and producing bogus failures.\n- I mutation-tested the harness (`to_ne_bytes` → `to_be_bytes`): it correctly failed, so the passes are not vacuous.\n\n**Phase D** — `run_all.sh` builds both libs, diffs `nm -D`, and runs the suite under every feature combo. `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` section, so `default` and `--no-default-features` are the complete set; both pass with an empty symbol diff. There is no binary target (`CMakeLists.txt` builds only a SHARED lib; `Cargo.toml` only a `cdylib`), so the stdout-comparison gate is covered by rows 15–18 comparing the libraries' actual stdout bytes.\n\nOnly changes made: added `libloading`/`libc` dev-deps, `tests/differential.rs`, the three markdown artifacts, and `run_all.sh`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the prescribed `build/` output dir was created).","ttft_ms":2485,"type":"result","duration_ms":341096,"uuid":"